.TITLE "diskutil"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Manages disks, volumes, partitions, and RAID sets on macOS. This command-line utility
provides extensive control over storage devices, including formatting, partitioning,
repairing, and mounting/unmounting volumes. It is the command-line equivalent
of Disk Utility.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**disktool**

.DIV "TLDR"
**diskutil list**
Lists all attached disks and their partitions.
> 

**diskutil mount __/dev/diskNsN__**
Mounts a specified volume, typically identified by its disk identifier (e.g., __/dev/disk1s2__).
> __/dev/diskNsN__: The identifier of the disk or volume.

**diskutil unmount __/Volumes/VolumeName__**
Unmounts a specified volume by its mount point.
> __/Volumes/VolumeName__: The mount point of the volume.

**diskutil eraseDisk __APFS__ __"MyDisk"__ __/dev/diskN__**
Erases and formats an entire physical disk with the __APFS__ filesystem and names it __"MyDisk"__.
> __APFS__: The filesystem to use (e.g., HFS+, APFS). | __"MyDisk"__: The new name for the disk. | __/dev/diskN__: The identifier of the physical disk.

**diskutil repairVolume __/Volumes/VolumeName__**
Repairs a specified volume, checking for and fixing errors in its filesystem.
> __/Volumes/VolumeName__: The mount point of the volume to repair.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Always use `diskutil` with caution, especially commands like `eraseDisk` and `partitionDisk`,
as they can lead to data loss if used incorrectly. It is highly recommended to
backup important data before performing any destructive operations.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:open**

documentation: https://ss64.com/osx/diskutil.html
